"text":"விற்","tr":"viṟ"}]},{"text":"காற்றாச்","tr":"kāṟṟāc","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"காற்","tr":"kāṟ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றாச்","tr":"ṟāc"}]},{"text":"சீறூர்த்","tr":"cīṟūrt","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"சீ","tr":"cī"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றூர்த்","tr":"ṟūrt"}]}],[{"text":"தொன்மை","tr":"toṉmai","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தொன்","tr":"toṉ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"மை","tr":"mai"}]},{"text":"சுட்டிய","tr":"cuṭṭiya","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"சுட்","tr":"cuṭ"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"டிய","tr":"ṭiya"}]},{"text":"வண்மை","tr":"vaṇmai","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"வண்","tr":"vaṇ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"மை","tr":"mai"}]},{"text":"யோனே","tr":"yōṉē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யோ","tr":"yō"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"னே","tr":"ṉē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"வேந்துடை","parts":[{"text":"வேந்துடை","lemma":"vēntuṭai","gloss":"having kings"}],"gloss":"having kings"},{"surface":"தானை","parts":[{"text":"தானை","lemma":"tāṉai","gloss":"army"}],"gloss":"army"},{"surface":"முனை","parts":[{"text":"முனை","lemma":"muṉai","gloss":"battlefront"}],"gloss":"battlefront"},{"surface":"கெட","parts":[{"text":"கெட","lemma":"keṭa","gloss":"to be ruined"}],"gloss":"to be ruined"},{"surface":"நெரிதர","parts":[{"text":"நெரிதர","lemma":"neritara","gloss":"to be crushed"}],"gloss":"to be crushed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஏந்து","parts":[{"text":"ஏந்து","lemma":"ēntu","gloss":"holding"}],"gloss":"holding"},{"surface":"வாள்","parts":[{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"vāḷ","gloss":"sword"}],"gloss":"sword"},{"surface":"வலத்தன்","parts":[{"text":"வலத்தன்","lemma":"valattaṉ","gloss":"strong man"}],"gloss":"strong man"},{"surface":"ஒருவன்","parts":[{"text":"ஒருவன்","lemma":"oruvaṉ","gloss":"one man"}],"gloss":"one man"},{"surface":"ஆகி","parts":[{"text":"ஆகி","lemma":"āki","gloss":"having become"}],"gloss":"having become"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"taṉ","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"இறந்து","parts":[{"text":"இறந்து","lemma":"iṟantu","gloss":"transgressing"}],"gloss":"transgressing"},{"surface":"வாராமை","parts":[{"text":"வாராமை","lemma":"vārāmai","gloss":"not coming"}],"gloss":"not coming"},{"surface":"விலக்கலின்","parts":[{"text":"விலக்கலின்","lemma":"vilakkal","gloss":"because of preventing"}],"gloss":"because of preventing"},{"surface":"பெரும்","parts":[{"text":"பெரும்","lemma":"perum","gloss":"great"}],"gloss":"great"},{"surface":"கடற்கு","parts":[{"text":"கடற்கு","lemma":"kaṭaṟku","gloss":"to the ocean"}],"gloss":"to the ocean"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆழி","parts":[{"text":"ஆழி","lemma":"āḻi","gloss":"shore"}],"gloss":"shore"},{"surface":"அனையன்","parts":[{"text":"அனையன்","lemma":"aṉaiyaṉ","gloss":"he who is like"}],"gloss":"he who is like"},{"surface":"மாதோ","parts":[{"text":"மாதோ","lemma":"mātō","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"என்றும்","parts":[{"text":"என்றும்","lemma":"eṉṟum","gloss":"always"}],"gloss":"always"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடி","parts":[{"text":"பாடி","lemma":"pāṭi","gloss":"having sung"}],"gloss":"having sung"},{"surface":"சென்றோர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"சென்றோர்க்கு","lemma":"ceṉṟōr","gloss":"to those who went"}],"gloss":"to those who went"},{"surface":"அன்றியும்","parts":[{"text":"அன்றியும்","lemma":"aṉṟiyum","gloss":"besides"}],"gloss":"besides"},{"surface":"வாரி","parts":[{"text":"வாரி","lemma":"vāri","gloss":"bounty"}],"gloss":"bounty"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புரவிற்கு","parts":[{"text":"புரவிற்கு","lemma":"puraviṟku","gloss":"to the patronage"}],"gloss":"to the patronage"},{"surface":"ஆற்றா","parts":[{"text":"ஆற்றா","lemma":"āṟṟā","gloss":"unable to sustain"}],"gloss":"unable to sustain"},{"surface":"சீறூர்","parts":[{"text":"சீறூர்","lemma":"cīṟūr","gloss":"small village"}],"gloss":"small village"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தொன்மை","parts":[{"text":"தொன்மை","lemma":"toṉmai","gloss":"ancient lineage"}],"gloss":"ancient lineage"},{"surface":"சுட்டிய","parts":[{"text":"சுட்டிய","lemma":"cuṭṭiya","gloss":"mindful of"}],"gloss":"mindful of"},{"surface":"வண்மையோனே","parts":[{"text":"வண்மையோனே","lemma":"vaṇmaiyōṉ","gloss":"generous man indeed"}],"gloss":"generous man indeed"}]}],"literal":"With the army of kings losing their front and being crushed / holding a raised sword, strong-armed, becoming a single man / preventing them from transgressing and coming past him, to the great ocean / he is like a shore indeed, always / not only to those who went singing, but also / of the small village unable to sustain giving / he is of generous nature, mindful of ancient lineage!","translation":"When the armies of kings are crushed and their battlefronts break, he stands alone, a single man with a raised sword in his strong hand. Preventing the enemy from passing beyond him, he is like a shore that restrains the great ocean. Not only to those who come singing his praise, but also to his small village that cannot afford to give, he is a man of generous nature, mindful of his ancient lineage!","modern":"மூவேந்தர்களின் படைகள் போர்க்களத்தில் சிதைந்து அழியும்போது, கையில் ஏந்திய வாளுடன் வலிமை மிக்க ஒருவனாக அவன் தனித்து நிற்கிறான். பகைவர்கள் தன்னைத் தாண்டிச் செல்லாதவாறு தடுப்பதில், அவன் பெரிய கடலைத் தடுக்கும் கரையைப் போன்றவன் ஆவான். தன்னைப் பாடி வரும் இரவலர்களுக்கு மட்டுமன்றி, பிறருக்குக் கொடுக்கும் வளம் இல்லாத தன் சிறிய ஊருக்கும், தன் குலத்தின் பழம்பெருமையை நினைத்து வாரி வழங்கும் வள்ளல் தன்மை கொண்டவன் அவன்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vaahai thinai and Mootin Mullai thurai, which praises the ancient martial lineage and bravery of a warrior. The poet, Madurai Kanakkayanar, describes a heroic warrior who stands alone on the battlefield with a raised sword, successfully blocking the advancing enemy forces. He is compared to a shore (aazhi) that restrains the vast, powerful ocean, symbolizing his immense strength and protective role. Beyond his martial valor, the warrior is also celebrated for his generosity; despite living in a small, resource-poor village (seerur), he continues to give abundantly to bards and his own community, honoring his family's ancient tradition of charity. Key words like 'aazhi' (shore/boundary), 'seerur' (small village), and 'vanmaiyone' (generous one) highlight the dual virtues of heroism and philanthropy.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.7],[1.7,2.1],[2.1,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,3.61],[3.67,4.0],[4.0,4.6],[4.6,4.8],[4.8,6.0],[6.0,6.3],[6.3,6.6],[6.6,7.6],[7.6,7.8],[7.8,8.1],[8.1,8.4],[8.4,9.44],[9.44,9.9],[9.9,10.3],[10.3,10.8],[10.8,10.8],[10.8,11.8],[12.34,12.38],[12.5,13.2],[13.2,13.3],[13.3,13.7],[13.7,14.0]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,1.9],[1.9,2.3],[2.3,3.3],[3.3,3.8],[3.8,3.8],[3.8,4.45],[5.11,5.33],[5.33,6.29],[6.29,6.9],[6.9,7.3],[7.3,7.8],[7.8,8.7],[8.7,8.9],[8.9,9.2],[9.2,9.6],[9.6,10.74],[10.74,11.2],[11.2,11.7],[11.7,12.2],[12.42,13.1],[13.1,13.47],[13.47,14.2],[14.2,14.9],[14.9,15.1],[15.1,15.5],[15.5,15.9]]},"sync":[[["வேந்துடை","having kings"]],[["தானை","army"]],[["முனை","battlefront"],["கெட","to be ruined"]],[["நெரிதர","to be crushed"]],[["ஏந்து","holding"],["வாள்","sword"]],[["வலத்தன்","strong man"]],[["ஒருவன்","one man"]],[["ஆகி","having become"]],[["தன்","his"],["இறந்து","transgressing"]],[["வாராமை","not coming"]],[["விலக்கலின்","because of preventing"]],[["பெரும்","great"]],[["கடற்கு","to the ocean"]],[["ஆழி","shore"]],[["அனையன்","he who is like"]],[["மாதோ","indeed"]],[["என்றும்","always"]],[["பாடி","having sung"]],[["சென்றோர்க்கு","to those who went"]],[["அன்றியும்","besides"]],[["வாரி","bounty"]],[["புரவிற்கு","to the patronage"]],[["ஆற்றா","unable to sustain"],["சீறூர்","small village"]],[["சீறூர்","small village"]],[["தொன்மை","ancient lineage"]],[["சுட்டிய","mindful of"]],[["வண்மையோனே","generous man indeed"]],[["வண்மையோனே","generous man indeed"]]]}